cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HebOCRBench, cite this software and the exact corpus/suite fingerprints reported by your run."
title: "HebOCRBench: A Multi-profile Hebrew OCR Benchmark"
version: 1.0.0
type: software
date-released: 2026-08-11
authors:
  - name: HebOCRBench contributors
repository-code: "https://github.com/office883/HebOCRBench"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - OCR
  - Modern Hebrew
  - Hebrew handwriting
  - historical Hebrew print
  - RTL
  - Unicode
  - document understanding
  - table recognition
  - robustness
abstract: >-
  HebOCRBench evaluates Hebrew OCR in logical Unicode order. It defines a
  guarded five-track Modern Hebrew print headline and reports handwriting,
  historical print and synthetic diagnostics as separate, non-blended
  families with explicit real-data coverage gaps.
